<title>ARGENTINA: Banco Frances completes sale to Bilbao Vizcaya.</title>
<headline>Banco Frances completes sale to Bilbao Vizcaya.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's Banco Frances del Rio de la Plata said Tuesday that it has completed a transfer of 30 percent of its shares to Spain's Banco de Bilbao Vizcaya SA in a deal worth $374.6 million.</p>
<p>The transfer was completed Monday, Banco Frances told the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange in a communique.  </p>
<p>Under the deal, Banco de Bilbao Vizcaya acquired all of  Inversora Otar SA, which controls  Sud America Inversiones SA. Sud America has 44 million shares of Banco Frances, representing 30 percent of the bank's shareholder equity.</p>
<p>-- Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650</p>
</text>
